      "title": "IEEE 802.15.4: fix null pointer in decryption.",
      "message": "IEEE 802.15.4: fix null pointer in decryption.\n\nCommit d6049d90d71de8d4c7a913327420b55e80a5c211 was trying to fix some\ncppcheck complaint by copying the generated key to decrypt_info->key,\nbut decrypt_info->key is initialized to null, so that crashed.\n\nRevert to setting decrypt_info->key to point to the on-the-stack key in\nquestion. That's safe, because the key is only used in routines called\nby decrypt_ieee802154_payload(), and decrypt_ieee802154_payload() sets\nthe pointer back to null before it returns.\n\nFixes d6049d90d71de8d4c7a913327420b55e80a5c211.\n",
      "author_name": "Guy Harris",
      "author_email": "gharris@sonic.net",
